<task id="to_log_in_to_xauthor_contracts_d4c842" xml:lang="en-us">
   <title>To log in to X-Author Contracts</title>
   <shortdesc>Chris Castro Launch Microsoft Word.</shortdesc>
   <prolog>
      <author type="creator">Chris Castro</author>
      <critdates>
         <revised modified="Sep 23, 2016"/>
      </critdates>
       <metadata>
      <keywords>
        <keyword>Author</keyword>
        <keyword>Contracts</keyword>
        <keyword>Launch</keyword>
        <keyword>document</keyword>
        <keyword>After</keyword>
        <keyword>login</keyword>
        <indexterm>Author</indexterm>
        <indexterm>Contracts</indexterm>
        <indexterm>Launch</indexterm>
      </keywords>
          <prodinfo>
        <prodname/>
      </prodinfo>
    </metadata>
  </prolog>
   <taskbody>
      <steps>
         <step>
            <cmd>Launch Microsoft Word. Open a new document or the document you want to work with.</cmd>
         </step>
         <step>
            <cmd>Launch the X-Author add-in as described in <xref href="../installing_x_author_contracts_45220121/installing_xauthor_contracts.dita">Installing X-Author Contracts</xref>.</cmd>
         </step>
         <step>
            <cmd>After the X-Author add-in pane loads, hover over the icon on the left-hand side to display the login menu.</cmd>
            <info>
               <fig>
                  <title>49676296</title>
                  <image href="../attachments/45711457/49676296.png" width="696" height="1278" placement="break">
                     <alt>placeholder</alt>
                  </image>
               </fig>
            </info>
         </step>
         <step>
            <cmd>Depending on the org you want to connect to, select <b>Sign-In to Production</b> or <b>Sign-In to Sandbox</b>.</cmd>
         </step>
         <step>
            <cmd>If it is the first time you are logging into the org, you will be prompted to allow X-Author to access Salesforce. Click <b>Allow</b> to proceed.</cmd>
         </step>
         <step>
            <cmd>Enter your Salesforce credentials to log in. After successful login, the X-Author pane refreshes and displays additional tabs.</cmd>
            <info>
               <fig>
                  <title>49676297</title>
                  <image href="../attachments/45711457/49676297.png" width="694" height="1278" placement="break">
                     <alt>placeholder</alt>
                  </image>
               </fig>
            </info>
         </step>
      </steps>
   </taskbody>
</task>